# UC06 — Multimodal Evidence Extraction

**Persona**: Advisory or forensic analyst working with messy, mixed-format source material.

**Scenario**: Source material includes a scanned old annual report (image-only PDF), a photographed whiteboard with figures, an Excel workbook where charts are pasted images, and handwritten analyst notes. Pull specific facts from each.

**Question types**:
- OCR-grade text extraction from scans
- Handwriting recognition
- Image-only chart interpretation
- Cross-modal reconciliation (handwritten notes vs typed report)

**Sample docs**: Scanned 1990s annual report from a public archive, whiteboard photo, multi-tab Excel with chart-as-image, 2–3 pages of original handwritten analyst notes.

**What this tests**: format coverage — exposes tools that can't ingest non-text inputs cleanly.
